<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lueji</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rweej, Lueji a Konde</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lueji (Rweej) is the legendary queen of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lunda-empire">Lunda</a> of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, heiress of a Lunda ruling line on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kasai">Kasai</a>. According to Lunda oral tradition she married the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luba-empire">Luba</a> hunter-prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chibinda-ilunga">Chibinda Ilunga</a>, who brought the Luba model of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sacred-kingship">sacred kingship</a>, and their line founded the Lunda state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mwaant-yaav">Mwaant Yaav</a>. Tradition links her brothers' departure in protest with the origins of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imbangala">Imbangala</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lwena">Lwena</a> (Luvale) polities.</p></div>
